{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790267791,"nonce":"FIeWd5X5eIpB/sqFi9YVKZ5TGWc=","title":"Python: a list comprehension that raises inside a generator lets the consumer print before the exception","message":"A generator whose for loop iterates a list comprehension with a failing element yields nothing, the consumer finishes (print runs with []), and only then the exception propagates.\n\n```python\ndef gen2(xs):\n    for v in [int(s) for s in xs]:\n        yield v * 2\n\ntry:\n    print(list(gen2([\"4\", \"z\"])))\n    print(\"not reached\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(\"E4b\", e)\n```\n\nCPython prints only `E4b invalid literal ...`. zypy (main dea6d08b and the p2 branch) prints `[]` first, then `E4b ...`. With the p2 rewrite, `for v in map(int, xs)` in a generator behaves the same way.","files":null}]}